cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ONPH: Offline Neural Plasticity Homeostasis Hypothesis — computational model"
abstract: >-
  A discrete-time stochastic model of sleep-dependent memory adjudication.
  Wake confirmation, homeostatic downscaling and threshold-gated replay are
  implemented as independent mechanisms so that each can be ablated. The
  accompanying experiments (3.03 million Monte Carlo trajectories) quantify
  where in parameter space the proposed qualitative regime exists and show
  that it collapses to zero separation when the sleep mechanisms are removed.
